WEBVTT

00:00:09.355 --> 00:00:10.395
TV JESSIE: They don't call this

00:00:10.475 --> 00:00:12.555
the old abandoned mine
for nothin', Prospector.

00:00:12.635 --> 00:00:14.395
I reckon we oughta get outta here.

00:00:14.475 --> 00:00:18.235
TV PETE: Where's my gold?
Hold on. I'll light me a candle.

00:00:18.315 --> 00:00:20.155
This sure is a fast-burnin' wick.

00:00:20.235 --> 00:00:23.155
Blast us to smithereens!
That there's dynamite!

00:00:23.235 --> 00:00:25.675
-Holy tarnation.
-I'll call for help.

00:00:25.795 --> 00:00:28.315
♪ Yodel-ay-hee-hoo ♪

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:31.635
Hey, critters, go get Sheriff Woody.
Now scurry!

00:00:33.155 --> 00:00:34.155
TV WOODY: Good job, Bullseye.

00:00:34.235 --> 00:00:36.475
I reckon the new schoolhouse
is finally done.

00:00:36.555 --> 00:00:38.595
-(CRITTERS CHITTERING)
-What's that?

00:00:38.675 --> 00:00:40.635
Jessie and Prospector are trapped
in the old abandoned mine,

00:00:40.715 --> 00:00:42.995
and Prospector just lit a stick
of dynamite thinkin' it was a candle,

00:00:43.115 --> 00:00:45.035
and now they're about
to be blown to smithereens?

00:00:45.115 --> 00:00:46.115
RABBIT: Mmm-hmm.

00:00:46.195 --> 00:00:48.675
Ride like the wind, Bullseye!

00:00:52.355 --> 00:00:56.595
You're fannin' the flames, Jessie!
It takes brains to put out that fire.

00:00:56.675 --> 00:00:59.075
Yow! My biscuits are burnin'!

00:01:04.115 --> 00:01:06.555
ANNOUNCER: Will Woody
and Bullseye land to safety?

00:01:06.635 --> 00:01:08.915
Can they reach Jessie
and Stinky Pete in time?

00:01:09.195 --> 00:01:13.235
Tune in next week for the exciting
conclusion, "Woody's Finest Hour."

00:01:13.475 --> 00:01:15.875
All right! All right! Next tape!

00:01:16.635 --> 00:01:18.835
Hey, wait.
What happened? What happens next?

00:01:18.915 --> 00:01:21.715
-Come on! Let's see the next episode!
-PETE: That's it.

00:01:21.795 --> 00:01:24.915
-What?
-The show was canceled after that.

00:01:25.795 --> 00:01:27.955
Wait. What about the gold mine

00:01:28.075 --> 00:01:30.435
and the cute little critters
and the dynamite?

00:01:30.515 --> 00:01:33.315
That was a great show!
I mean, why cancel it?

00:01:33.395 --> 00:01:35.835
Two words, Sput-nik.

00:01:35.915 --> 00:01:40.795
Once the astronauts went up, children
only wanted to play with space toys.

00:01:40.875 --> 00:01:44.355
I know how that feels.
But, still, my own show.

00:01:44.435 --> 00:01:46.955
-I mean, look at all this stuff!
-JESSIE: Didn't you know?

00:01:47.195 --> 00:01:49.515
Why, you're valuable property!

00:01:49.595 --> 00:01:52.675
I wish the guys could see this.
Hey-howdy-hey. That's me.

00:01:52.755 --> 00:01:55.475
I'm on a yo-yo. (CHUCKLES)

00:01:55.555 --> 00:01:59.835
Oh, hey. Nice teeth.
And yet still a good-lookin' guy.

00:02:02.915 --> 00:02:05.515
Oh, it's a bank! Cool.

00:02:06.155 --> 00:02:08.795
What do you do?
You push the hat, and out...

00:02:08.875 --> 00:02:12.195
Oh, out come bubbles. Clever.

00:02:12.275 --> 00:02:14.755
Oh, wow. Hey, what's this thing do?

00:02:16.115 --> 00:02:18.515
(LAUGHING) I get it.

00:02:18.595 --> 00:02:20.595
"There's a snake in my boot."

00:02:20.675 --> 00:02:24.155
Oh, hey, Bullseye.
Go long! Go long! Whoo!

00:02:25.835 --> 00:02:28.755
-(DISTORTED INSTRUMENTAL)
-A record player!

00:02:28.835 --> 00:02:30.835
I haven't seen one of these in ages.

00:02:31.435 --> 00:02:33.555
(FAST-SPEED YODELING)

00:02:33.635 --> 00:02:35.675
-(SINGING SLOWS)
-Okay, now. Slow.

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:38.715
-(EXTRA-SLOW SINGING)
-Oh, that's funny, Bullseye.

00:02:38.955 --> 00:02:41.515
Hop on, cowgirl! Think fast!

00:02:41.595 --> 00:02:43.675
JESSIE: (GASPS) Oh.

00:02:44.355 --> 00:02:45.355
Not bad.

00:02:45.435 --> 00:02:47.195
♪ It's time for Woody's Roundup

00:02:47.275 --> 00:02:49.195
-Whee!
-♪ He's the very best

00:02:49.275 --> 00:02:52.595
(FAST-SPEED) ♪ He's the rootin'-est
tootin'-est cowboy... ♪

00:02:53.235 --> 00:02:55.915
Look at us! We're a complete set!

00:02:55.995 --> 00:02:59.075
-Now it's on to the museum.
-Museum?

00:02:59.155 --> 00:03:01.755
-(RECORD SCRATCHING)
-(JESSIE SCREAMING)

00:03:01.835 --> 00:03:03.795
-What museum?
-PETE: THE museum.

00:03:03.875 --> 00:03:07.875
We're being sold
to the Konishi Toy Museum in Tokyo.

00:03:07.955 --> 00:03:10.155
-That's in Japan!
-Japan?

00:03:10.235 --> 00:03:12.835
No, no, no, no, no. I can't go to Japan.

00:03:12.915 --> 00:03:15.235
(CHUCKLES) What do you mean?

00:03:15.315 --> 00:03:19.075
I got to get back home to
my owner, Andy. Hey, look, look. See?

00:03:19.155 --> 00:03:22.115
-(GASPS) He still has an owner.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:03:22.195 --> 00:03:25.555
(HYPERVENTILATING) No. Can't go.

00:03:26.235 --> 00:03:28.395
I can't do storage again. I just can't!

00:03:28.475 --> 00:03:30.635
-Jessie. Jessie.
-I won't go back in the dark!

00:03:31.195 --> 00:03:32.635
What's the matter?
What's wrong with her?

00:03:32.715 --> 00:03:35.595
Well, we've been in storage
for a long time

00:03:35.675 --> 00:03:36.715
waiting for you.

00:03:37.235 --> 00:03:39.115
-Why me?
-The museum's

00:03:39.195 --> 00:03:42.395
only interested in the collection
if you're in it, Woody.

00:03:43.075 --> 00:03:45.755
Without you, we go back into storage.

00:03:46.275 --> 00:03:48.875
-It's that simple.
-It's not fair!

00:03:48.955 --> 00:03:50.315
How can you do this to us?

00:03:50.395 --> 00:03:53.235
Hey, look. I'm sorry,
but this is all a big mistake.

00:03:53.315 --> 00:03:56.475
-You see, I was in this yard sale...
-Yard sale?

00:03:56.555 --> 00:03:58.755
Why were you in a yard sale
if you have an owner?

00:03:58.835 --> 00:04:01.755
Well, I wasn't supposed to be there.
I was trying to save another toy when...

00:04:01.835 --> 00:04:05.515
Was it because you're damaged?
Hmm? Did this Andy break you?

00:04:05.875 --> 00:04:09.475
Yeah, but... No, no, no, no, no!
It was... It was an accident.

00:04:09.555 --> 00:04:12.155
-I mean...
-Sounds like he really loves you.

00:04:12.235 --> 00:04:16.115
It's not like that, okay?
And I'm not going to any museum!

00:04:16.195 --> 00:04:19.035
-Well, I'm not going back into storage!
-(DOOR OPENING)

00:04:19.115 --> 00:04:21.155
-(GASPS)
-PETE: Al's coming!

00:04:21.235 --> 00:04:23.675
-(GASPS)
-Go! Go on, Jessie.

00:04:23.755 --> 00:04:25.235
-Oh...
-Jessie, look at me.

00:04:25.515 --> 00:04:29.195
I promise you'll come out of the box.
Now go! Go!

00:04:31.515 --> 00:04:33.195
(AL HUMMING)

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:37.755
It's show time!

00:04:38.195 --> 00:04:41.875
(CHUCKLES) Oh, money, baby.
Money, money, money.

00:04:42.075 --> 00:04:43.715
(LAUGHS EVILLY)

00:04:43.795 --> 00:04:45.035
And now

00:04:45.115 --> 00:04:46.755
the main attraction.

00:04:46.835 --> 00:04:48.595
(RESUMES HUMMING)

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:58.195
(GASPS, SCREAMS)

00:04:58.275 --> 00:05:00.795
No! His arm! Where's his arm?

00:05:01.795 --> 00:05:04.795
Oh... No. No, no, no, no!

00:05:04.915 --> 00:05:07.555
What am I gonna do? I know. I know.

00:05:07.635 --> 00:05:11.275
(MUTTERING) Come on! Come on!
Come on! Pick up the phone!

00:05:11.355 --> 00:05:12.835
-MAN: Hello?
-It's me. It's Al.

00:05:12.915 --> 00:05:14.075
I got an emergency.

00:05:14.155 --> 00:05:15.875
-I'm busy.
-Yes, we're all busy.

00:05:15.955 --> 00:05:18.795
-Look. It has to be tonight.
-(MAN RESPONDS, INDISTINCT)

00:05:18.875 --> 00:05:21.115
All right. All right.
But first thing in the morning.

00:05:21.635 --> 00:05:23.995
(SCREAMS) It's gone! I can't believe it!

00:05:24.195 --> 00:05:26.675
-My arm is completely gone!
-All right. Come here. Let me see that.

00:05:26.755 --> 00:05:29.075
-(GASPING)
-Oh, it's just a popped seam,

00:05:29.155 --> 00:05:30.315
easily repaired.

00:05:30.395 --> 00:05:32.435
-You should consider yourself lucky.
-Lucky?

00:05:32.515 --> 00:05:35.635
Are you shrink-wrapped?
I am missing my arm!

00:05:35.715 --> 00:05:37.035
Big deal.

00:05:39.635 --> 00:05:42.435
Let him go. I'm sure his precious Andy

00:05:42.515 --> 00:05:45.835
is dying to play with
a one-armed cowboy doll.

00:05:46.275 --> 00:05:50.155
Why, Jessie, you know he wouldn't last
an hour on the streets in his condition.

00:05:50.235 --> 00:05:53.795
It's a dangerous world
out there for a toy.

00:05:58.315 --> 00:05:59.675
(OWL HOOTING)

00:06:04.515 --> 00:06:05.795
(GASPING)

00:06:09.275 --> 00:06:10.315
(CHUCKLES)

00:06:16.635 --> 00:06:19.275
All right.
Nobody look till I get my cork back in.

00:06:19.355 --> 00:06:22.715
Good work, men. Two blocks down
and only 19 more to go.

00:06:22.795 --> 00:06:24.035
-What?
-ALL: Nineteen?

00:06:24.115 --> 00:06:26.595
Are we gonna do this all night?
My parts are killing me.

00:06:26.675 --> 00:06:27.755
Come on, fellas.

00:06:27.835 --> 00:06:31.235
Did Woody give up when Sid
had me strapped to a rocket?

00:06:31.315 --> 00:06:32.955
-ALL: No.
-No.

00:06:33.035 --> 00:06:35.955
And did he give up when you threw him
out of the back of that moving van?

00:06:36.035 --> 00:06:38.275
-Oh, you had to bring that up.
-No, he didn't!

00:06:38.835 --> 00:06:43.795
We have a friend in need, and we will
not rest until he's safe in Andy's room!

00:06:43.875 --> 00:06:45.715
-(INSPIRATIONAL MUSIC PLAYING)
-Now let's move out!

00:06:51.555 --> 00:06:54.475
ANNOUNCER: And that concludes
our broadcast day.

00:06:54.555 --> 00:06:55.555
(STATIC)

00:06:57.875 --> 00:06:59.115
(SNORING)

00:07:11.755 --> 00:07:12.715
(SNORTING)

00:07:18.755 --> 00:07:19.755
(CRUNCHING)

